KZ3 patch 4024: a cellFsOpen pre-open hook (KZ3 only). A port hook is told the guest path and the resolved host path
before cellFsOpen stats or opens anything. port/net/kz3_fios_stamp.h uses it on the first open of FIOS's disk cache
(/dev_hdd1/cache/<title>/fios/cache.idx or cache.dat): a cache built by another port build or other KZ3_ switches
holds blocks of disc files the port rewrites (menu pages), FIOS treats a changed disc file as a failed read, and the
menu request fails with GUM error 20000 (network pass 41, the RE notes s.35). The hook removes that cache first, as
FIOS does with a cache it rejects (patch 4018), so FIOS builds a new one. The hook must be quick and must not block.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 153): hunks unchanged; offsets and context follow the v0.19.0 chain (group A r152 files, Toro v019-c, R&C v019-b where delivered; originals for the rest, three-way merged where they did not apply).

